stry","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[routing_anti_patterns_registry].principle_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime].principle_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"sleeper_memory_poisoning_quarantine_replay","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[sleeper_memory_poisoning_quarantine_replay].principle_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"tool_server_pressure_inventory","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[tool_server_pressure_inventory].principle_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop].principle_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"world_model_projection_drift_control_room","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[world_model_projection_drift_control_room].principle_refs"}],"cited_by_count":36,"component_ids":["batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule","batch10_governance_compilers_capsule","batch10_live_source_drift_capsule","batch11_saturation_engines_capsule","batch12_market_dashboard_read_model_capsule","batch12_prediction_market_board_capsule","batch4_proof_authority_runtime","batch5_authority_systems_capsule","batch6_unsurfaced_primitives_capsule","batch7_demo_take_console_capsule","batch7_macro_engines_capsule","batch7_oracle_sibling_capsule","batch7_secondary_runtime_capsule","batch8_audio_level_rms_port","batch8_compliance_pipeline_capsule","batch8_policy_engines_capsule","batch8_structural_theses_capsule","batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","batch8_validator_checker_capsule","batch9_macro_engines_capsule","bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","cognitive_operator_registry","cold_reader_route_map","engine_room_demo","indirect_prompt_injection_information_flow_policy_replay","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","prediction_oracle_reconciliation","public_reveal_walkthrough","routing_anti_patterns_registry","semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","sleeper_memory_poisoning_quarantine_replay","tool_server_pressure_inventory","voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":[],"id":"P-9","kind":"principle","plain":"Every piece of data that moves out of the private source system, a fixture, a result record, public copy, a provider's response format or material stored next to the private root must carry a label saying where it came from and how strongly it may be claimed. If the flow is only declared, or labelled only at its end, say so.","principles":[],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The parcel picture covers only the difference between a label added at the end and a record carried all the way; an intact seal still says nothing about whether the contents are right.","maps":[{"analogy":"the parcel carries its custody log through every handoff","doctrine":"a value carries its origin class across each boundary"},{"analogy":"the tamper seal is applied when packed and stays intact","doctrine":"the usage limit travels with the value from the start"},{"analogy":"a sticker added at the last dock is logged as a late sticker","doctrine":"a label added only at the destination is recorded as such"}],"text":"A parcel carries a custody log and a tamper seal applied where it was packed. If a clean sticker was added at the last loading dock instead, the log has to say so."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A public page prints a value copied from a source next to private files because the final copy step looked clean, with no origin record carried across the copy.","does_not_prove":"Catching labelled flows at named boundaries covers those boundaries only, and full tracking across every path is a recorded open gap.","enforced_in_component_ids":["indirect_prompt_injection_information_flow_policy_replay","macro_projection_import_protocol"],"example":{"component_ids":["indirect_prompt_injection_information_flow_policy_replay"],"text":"The prompt-injection replay keeps the information-flow policy attached to the data, so untrusted instructions arriving at a tool call are caught at that boundary even though they reached a trusted endpoint."},"governs":"Every boundary a value crosses on its way from imported source to a public or privileged destination.","plain":"A value carries a record of where it came from and how far it may be used, and that record travels with it through every handoff. If something was only labelled clean at the final step, that has to be written down.","potential_misread":"That a clean label at the destination is enough, whether or not it travelled with the value through the earlier boundaries.","refuses":"Taking a clean label at the destination as evidence when it was added there and never travelled with the value.","requires":"An origin class and a usage limit carried with the value across each crossing, and a note whenever a flow is only declared or labelled at the destination.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"A clean-looking final copy can still be treated as unchecked, so trust depends on where a value came from."},"rests_on":["AX-8"],"source_ref":"PRINCIPLES.md::P-9","statement":"Grounding: AX-8.\nObligation grounding: AX-8.O1.label_propagation, AX-8.O2.sink_policy, AX-8.O3.lying_endpoint_rejected.\n\nEvery piece of data that moves out of the private source system, a fixture, a\nresult record, public copy, a provider's response format or material stored next\nto the private root must carry a label saying where it came from and how\nstrongly it may be claimed. If the flow is only declared, or labelled only at\nits end, say so.","statement_sha256":"eddf0b30e1d2f85dbb81b89772187b1f50db06c6224916178484b6fd59ac2c63","title":"Preserve provenance across every boundary","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}